"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both Goldman Sachs and Morgan Stanley disclose that expanding their business activities exposes them to risks from transacting with a broader or different array of clients and counterparties. GS notes it faces 'enhanced risks as we operate in new locations and transact with a broader array of clients and counterparties.' Similarly, MS states that business initiatives 'may change our client or account profile or bring us into contact... with individuals and entities that are not within our traditional client and counterparty base,' exposing it to 'new and enhanced risks, greater regulatory scrutiny... increased credit-related... and operational risks.' While GS specifically highlights 'new locations' and MS highlights 'new products' and 'regulatory scrutiny,' both frame the risk around the inherent dangers of broadening the scope of client and counterparty relationships.",
