{
"peer_ticker": "C",
"peer_disclosure_id": "c_2024_1A_D030",
"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both Goldman Sachs and Citigroup identify counterparty concentrations and the breadth of their counterparty base as a source of significant risk. GS warns of 'enhanced risks' from transacting with a 'broader array of... counterparties.' Citi elaborates on this by stating that 'concentrations of risk to clients or counterparties... can also increase Citi's risk of significant losses,' specifically citing 'high volume of transactions' with 'counterparties in the financial services industry' and the danger of 'rapid deterioration' in sectors or geographies where it has large exposures. Both companies acknowledge that the diversity and volume of their counterparty relationships create material exposure to potential losses.",
